    <!-- The name of your plugin that will appear in the plugin list -->
    <FriendlyName>TODO Undo</FriendlyName>

    <!-- The author name that you want to appear in the plugin list -->
    <Author>Viktor Ferenczi</Author>

    <!-- Optional tooltip for the plugin in the plugin list -->
    <Tooltip>Ctrl-Z undoes and Ctrl-Y redoes block building, painting, grid paste and delete, terminal changes and text edits</Tooltip>

    <!-- Optional plugin description. If omitted, this will be the same as the Tooltip. 1000 characters max. -->
    <Description>Undo and redo for ship design.

        Ctrl-Z reverts the last operation in the current context and Ctrl-Y applies it again.
        Covered: placing and removing blocks, painting and skins, pasting and deleting grids,
        terminal property changes, block and grid names, programmable block programs and
        single line text fields. Vanilla uses Ctrl-Z for relative dampeners and Ctrl-Y for
        toggling all reactors; those move to Ctrl-Shift-Z and Ctrl-Shift-Y. All bindings
        and limits can be changed in the plugin settings.

        The history is saved with the world and follows its backups. Works offline, when
        hosting for friends, and as far as the server allows when connected to a server.
        In survival only what a player could do anyway can be undone unless creative tools
        are enabled.
    </Description>

